    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0569" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg527"/>

                <head>Lord Lyons to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 23, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: A British subject has written to
                    ask me to inquire from you whether you will grant permits to British subjects to
                    load ships with cotton in the Savannah river below the confederate obstructions.
                    Will you be so kind as to tell me what answer I should make ?</p>
                <p>Yours, faithfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
